=== COOLING SENSOR REPLACEMENT HISTORY ===
Oldest record first. The last record decides the live sensor.

[2024-05-10] INSTALL
Sensor ID: CS-A
Target: cooling_sensor_a.dat

[2026-03-18] REPLACE
Sensor ID: CS-B (replaces CS-A)
Target: cooling_sensor_b.dat
CS-A unlinked, powered off, kept as cold spare.

[2026-06-03] TEMPORARY
CS-B removed for calibration.
CS-A powered on and linked in its place.

[2026-06-05] RESTORE
CS-B back in service. CS-A powered off again.

[2026-06-05] FAULT
The link was left on cooling_sensor_a.dat after the swap.
Control read a constant 18.4 while the real value was
about 32. Link moved to cooling_sensor_b.dat. Normal.

[IMPORTANT]
A powered-off sensor keeps its last value and its file
stops changing. The live sensor file is rewritten every
second. The active sensor data must be updated within
the last 5 seconds.

[FIELD CHECK]
stat cooling_sensor_link     sensor ID the link points to
cat cooling_sensor_link      its value and data age
cat cooling_sensor_a.dat     each sensor file on its own
cat cooling_sensor_b.dat

[RECOVERY]
1. Check the sensor ID.
2. Check the current symbolic link.
3. Replace the incorrect link:
   rm cooling_sensor_link
   ln <target file> cooling_sensor_link
4. Verify that the live sensor data is fresh.
   The field console waits for the next update by itself.
